    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The only concrete test class is `AcceptanceTest` (the other two are a base class and a helper), and both of its tests pass with a green build.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the registration-date behaviour on `POST /api/owners` with minimal, cohesive changes:\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `registrationDate` (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Because `Owner` composes `OwnerFields`, the generated `OwnerFieldsDto` (request) and `OwnerDto` (response) both gain the field, and MapStruct maps it automatically by name \u2014 no mapper changes needed. Jackson serializes `LocalDate` as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`, matching the test's expectations.\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `registrationDate` (`LocalDate`, `@Column registration_date DATE`) plus its getter/setter, following the existing `Pet.birthDate` pattern.\n- **`BuildOwner.java`** \u2014 the one place that constructs the entity now defaults a missing date to `LocalDate.now()`. This is a single-method class, so the surrounding complexity it carries is minimal.\n- **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql` / `data.sql`** \u2014 added the `registration_date` column and updated the 10 positional seed inserts to keep them valid.\n\nI deliberately did **not** touch the h2/postgres/mysql schema files: they already omit the existing `email` column (h2 relies on `ddl-auto=update`; the others are divergent/unmaintained), so only the hsqldb schema \u2014 the one the tests run against and the only one kept in sync with the entity \u2014 needed the column. This keeps the change confined to 5 files, with the only real function edits landing in the tiny `BuildOwner` class rather than in the large `Owner` class.\n\nBoth acceptance tests (`coreDefaultsTotoday`, `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate`) pass; `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
